def row(source,ids,challenge,decision):
 rows.append(dict(source=source,question_ids=ids.split(),challenged_clause=challenge,adjudication=decision,status='ACTUALLY_TESTED'))
row('Law1.1–1.6,1.10–1.16; Playbook6–7','Q021 Q022 Q083','First/later setup token state, bank player-count branch, saved map order and resource shortfall actor.','Keys specify normal banners at one, 3 versus 4 per bank, board resources/full Supply, top Cradle two purple, other faceup suited-card sites one, ruin-only exclusion, Chancellor favor-shortfall allocation, and Round1/Visions0. This goes beyond naming Setup.')
row('Law1.7–1.9,1.13–1.15,1.23; Playbook6–7,30','Q023 Q102','Inherited board eligibility versus chosen Chancellor and random seating; arbitrary pawn starts.','Keys distinguish any Chancellor selection from previous-winner recommendation, random other seats from fixed first-game order, board choice in turn order on Chronicled side, any faceup non-Chancellor pawn site, top Cradle Chancellor pawn, and banner/title assignment. Starting Citizen gets no relic.')
row('Law1.17–1.23 and deferred-rebuild box; errata1.17','Q024 Q101','Relic positions, bottom-deck starting cards, and prerequisite timing when previous Chronicle omitted rebuild.','Q024 tests random one-per-Reliquary-space placement, bottom three total discard seeds, three bottom cards per player, pawn-before-discard region, facedown choice and drawn Vision count. Q101 explicitly forbids seeding/dealing before deferred rebuild.')
row('Playbook6–7 setup1–18 and diagrams; Playbook8','Q025 Q084 Q103','First packet preparation must differ from later-game bottom dealing, random preparation and freely chosen Oath.','Keys expressly require faceup three named sites and their denizens, facedown other sites/advisers/Ivory Eye, correct pawn and garrison locations, 3/3/5 discards, ordered 41-card deck, assigned advisers, 4 Reliquary/15 remaining relics and fixed Supremacy. Original diagrams visually corroborate orientations.')
row('Law2.1–2.9; errata2.8/Rule; Playbook8','Q008 Q010 Q012 Q014 Q019 Q066 Q096','Components must imply operative access, counting and capacity consequences, not inventory memorization.','Keys test draw sources, adviser count and no facedown properties, printed target shields, unavailable Reliquary relic powers/goals/theft, faceup-only rule, no facedown-site cards, one-color site occupancy, pawn-independent garrison rule, ruin capacity/no-suit/no-Muster-or-Trade while retaining power.')
row('Law2.11; errata2.11','Q001 Q036 Q088','Incumbent tie privilege, simultaneous successor holders, and title timing during Campaign.','Q036 asks both incumbent tie and tied new leaders, gives incumbent choice only after falling behind, Oathkeeper-side receipt and transfer after Campaign ends. Q088 requires 1/2 defense dice, Campaign modifier status and Imperial sharing, rather than merely naming the title.')
row('Law3.1–3.4; errata3.2','Q001 Q002 Q003 Q004 Q005 Q074','Every win route, side restriction, strict-most threshold and endgame priority.','Keys distinguish check-before-flip, two-Wake Usurper path, revealed complete Vision plus three world Visions, strict most not tied, 5/6/7 die thresholds with Imperial title gate, all four Successor mappings, and Empire/Usurper/Vision-priority/Empire fallback at automatic round8. Citizen substitution is solo and applies in either Empire branch.')
row('Law4 introductory paragraph,4.1–4.3; Playbook10','Q006 Q007 Q068 Q083 Q092 Q095','Full turn and round order; optional actions cannot interrupt another action or be moved to Wake.','Keys give Chancellor-first clockwise rounds, Wake/Act/Rest, check before advancing round marker, zero/repeated/ordered actions only while payable, finish each action, and ordinary mandatory Wake versus optional Rest and explicitly optional income.')
row('Law4.1.1','Q006 Q072','Mob threshold, repeat ordering, tied poorest banks and one-favor floor.','Q006 directly tests poorest-bank tie choice, forced addition if able at one, no loss of last favor, repeat only if already Mob, then threshold check. Q072 is useful regression arithmetic but has no new credited operator.')
row('Law4.3.1–4.3.5; errata4.3.3; Playbook3 boards','Q007 Q079','Resource return locations, supply actor distinction, saved Supply and refresh cap.','Q007 specifies each card class for favor/secrets, faceup own exhausted secrets, personal-bank count for Exile/Chancellor, exact Chancellor marker for Citizens including leftmost, saved remaining Supply and cap, then optional Rest powers once each. Q079 supplies board brackets without new novelty credit.')
row('Law5.1.1–5.1.3; Playbook12,32; errataDraw','Q008 Q009 Q067 Q082','Mandatory draw count versus voluntary stop, world Vision versus discard Vision, exhaustion and generic Draw.','Q008 already gives one-source selection, discard2/world2-3-4/DarkestSecret2, prescribed count, source shortfall, world one-at-time announcement/stop/track, no discard Vision stop/track, discard before play. Q067 separately tests corrected generic Draw not importing Search stop; Q082 remains zero-credit regression.')
row('Law5.1.4.I–III,6.1,7.2,7.6.4; errata7.6.4','Q010 Q030 Q076','Site/adviser/revealed-Vision destinations, facedown future play and capacity-before-play.','Keys require legal restrictions, suited site reward, adviser capacity including facedown, prospective lowest new limit before play, locked protection, facedown minor play/discard and true Vision replacement outside advisers. Q076 requires both People’s Favor sites in pawn region, different sites allowed, no locked discard and receiving capacity.')
row('Law5.1.4.IV; Card Reference Conspiracy','Q031 Q069','Conspiracy actor, theft conditions, non-enemy target, actual optional effect and final cleanup.','Q031 states anyone including Imperials, co-located target, two matching own faceup advisers possibly matching same opponent adviser, one-secret burn, one relic/banner, target need not enemy, no revealed-Vision replacement, box even without theft, and banner seizure. Q069 generalizes seizure outside Campaign.')
row('Law5.2–5.3; Law9.3','Q011 Q026 Q062 Q087','Muster and both Trade operators must test costs, card occupancy/type, locality and source destination.','Q011 requires pawn-site empty denizen/intact edifice, excludes relic/ruin, pays Supply and resources, puts two gained personal-bank warbands on board (purple for Citizen), and applies matching faceup advisers to each Trade formula with zero-match secret result and source shortfall. Access to remote powers does not permit remote board actions.')
row('Law5.4; errata5.4; banner placards','Q012 Q013','Recover targets, outbidding, safe Darkest Secret conditions, old token destinations and banner reset.','Q012 requires facedown local relic and printed site cost versus banner from anywhere/self, strict resource outbid, faceup holding, People’s Favor normal-side reset and cyclic old-favor distribution, DarkestSecret one to new holder/rest previous holder/self all. Q013 tests empty/ruin-only safety, suited mismatch, no-adviser correction and self/shared-bank exceptions.')
row('Law5.5.1–5.5.2; errata5.5.2','Q014 Q015 Q017','Legal defender, local compulsory target, remote target freedom and corrected attacking-force ceiling.','Q014 tests defender rule or pawn at attacker site, bandits only if no player rule, compulsory site if defender rules, at least one local target, co-located relic satisfying local requirement, remote defender sites, pawn/relic/banner locality and target shield contributions. Q015 uses corrected force ceiling, normally board warbands, permitting power-expanded force.')
row('Law5.5.1–5.5.4 Empire clauses; errataCampaign power-sharing','Q017 Q070 Q081 Q088','Allied actor permissions, personal locations, sidewide prohibitions and temporary Imperial exclusions.','Keys distinguish Citizen attacking either Imperial and Chancellor attacking Citizen, automatic Chancellor ally, willing eligible non-attacker Citizen allies, defender permission/location, own advisers versus shared Imperial-site plans, user payment and one total use, board-force locality, declared-defender contested priority, sidewide you/defender versus individual your board/site, title sharing outside Supremacy, and enemy identities including bandits.')
row('Law5.5.3;7.5.1–7.5.4; Card Reference icons','Q027 Q037 Q080 Q094','Battle-plan rule-only access, role colors, payment exception, order, zero-pool conversion and free bandit plans.','Keys require attacker then defender, ruled plans once each, all free ruled bandit plans, occupied-card payment allowed, off-turn favor immediately bank/secret exhausted on own board, role-correct red/blue/gradient, independently chosen +/- sign on printed die type, and defense die addition when attack die removed from empty pool.')
row('Law5.5.4–5.5.6; errataforce; Law9.5','Q015 Q038 Q039 Q078 Q090','Defense arithmetic domain, skull timing, hollow swords, force sacrifice and defeated attacker/defender.','Q015 explicitly doubles only shields exponentially, adds targeted garrisons/qualified board force, immediately kills own force for skulls, pairs hollow swords, requires strict attack advantage, permits exact winning sacrifice only. Q038 tests halving remaining force after skulls with rounded-down loss and no winning-defender booty. Q090 tests purple kills to Chancellor bank, separating survivors to boards.')
row('Law5.5.6–5.5.8; errata5.5.7.I relocation','Q016 Q017 Q077 Q093','Mandatory/optional target resolution and both battle outcomes, with victory and discard timing.','Keys give defeat half-down/survivors/defeated effects, Chancellor loss choice, site survivors to Chancellor board and Citizen board survivors staying, optional zero garrisons, mandatory all relic/banner taking and seizure penalty, independent optional banish/favor burn, legal no-Supply travel with Wood destination priority, then winner effects and either-side end-discard. Q093 explicitly tests victorious defender and losing attacker cleanup.')
row('Law5.6;7.6.2; errataTravel','Q018 Q054 Q055 Q056 Q057 Q060 Q063','Entire directed travel matrix, reveal prompts and fixed/increase/free ordering.','Q018 tests all Cradle/Provinces/Hinterland costs, pawn movement without garrisons, reveal favor/secrets/relics and fixed-number before other modifiers, with no-Supply overriding increases. Site keys test the named restriction/destination exceptions, not just regional routes.')
row('Law6.3–6.5;7.6.5; Grand Scepter printed power','Q032 Q033 Q065','Minor peeks and warband movement versus forbidden ordinary occupation and last-warband removal.','Keys require local unpeeked relic access, later remote reinspection of specific previously peeked relic, Scepter Reliquary access subject taken-this-turn prohibition, ordinary pickups leaving one and ruled-site dropoff, Chancellor Citizen pickup permission, consensual co-located Imperial board transfers, and BanditCrown virtual-bandit exception without expendability.')
row('Law6.6–6.8;7.6.1; Grand Scepter','Q019 Q034 Q035 Q071 Q086','Citizenship offer versus forced conversion versus exile/self-exile, including turn endings and garrisons.','Keys test Scepter holder even Exile self-offer, exactly one Reliquary relic plus optional listed binding exchange, purple shortage choice, Vision discard, held Usurper reset, full Supply and end Act only on recipient turn. Forced power skips offer requirements. Exiling others uses five favor adjusted by both holders’ title/banner, converts board only and does not automatically end Act; self-exile counts all placed secrets plus board warbands, bars Scepter holder and ends Act.')
row('Law7.1–7.4; Card Reference Rules of Use','Q026 Q027 Q028 Q029 Q030 Q087 Q095','Power access, payment, occupancy, persistence, required resolution, timing and modifier lifetime.','Keys explicitly test rule-or-pawn access, persistent thick-braid ignoring access for described players, occupied-card placement prohibition/no-cost exception, burned versus placed payment, no facedown secret payment, resolve as much as possible even zero effect, explicit may, restriction banners only faceup, site/adviser/locked constraints, mandatory WhenPlayed after reward/Homeland/modifiers, once-per-Wake/Rest, action-start modifier ordering, one current-action use and active-discard protection.')
row('Law7.6.3;9.6; Site Reference Tribunal','Q043 Q064 Q100','Ordinary nonbinding promises versus enumerated binding permissions and optional Exchange operator.','Keys test no unprompted resource gifts, only named binding exceptions/if able, exclusive Citizenship exchange of Reliquary relics, Tribunal immediate favor/secrets plus future actions and disputed breach coin flip, remote ruler/local pawn access, and Exchange as optional bilateral Give with no invented equality/simultaneity.')
row('Law8.1–8.2; errata8.2','Q020 Q075','New Oath branching and Chronicle-specific Citizenship rather than ordinary offer rules.','Q020 already distinguishes Vision-alone matching Oath from any-other/multiple-method different Oath, all Citizen boards even boxed flip when Exile wins, excludes just-flipped and self, optional other Exiles, one winner warband per accepted ruled site and no ordinary Reliquary offer.')
row('Law8.3.1; Playbook4 embedded Chronicle aid','Q045','Winner role, optional one edifice build/repair and occupied-site exclusion.','Q045 explicitly tests Imperial winner only, one build or repair, winner-ruled site, new matching-suit Archive replacement with denizen to world deck, no intact/ruined edifice already at build site, or repair existing ruled ruin.')
row('Law8.3.2–8.3.4; errata8.3.3','Q046 Q104','Retain/discard branches, exact actual-flip denizen-discard guard and retained ruin attachments.','Q046 key explicitly restricts this ruining-step discard to sites where an intact edifice actually flipped, retains corrected denizen attachments on set-aside ruins, separates discarded-site denizens/relics/ruins destinations, and removes map pawns/resources/warbands. Q104 repeats the actual-flip guard under supplied retention; retain regression, zero extra novelty on this frozen key.')
row('Law8.3.5','Q047','Compaction must preserve directional ordering, ruin reverse insertion and guaranteed faceup regions.','Q047 gives Cradle fill from Cradle then Provinces then Hinterland top-down, Provinces then Hinterland, Hinterland push, saved ruins bottom-up into Hinterland then Provinces bottom-up, remaining facedown draws, and top-site flip for region with no faceup site. Further map permutations instantiate the same ordered operator.')
row('Law8.4; Law10 Gain; Law9.3; Law10 map suit cycle','Q048 Q049','Winner adviser suit/ties/no suited advisers, clockwise allocation and total alternate healing procedure.','Keys specify 3/2/1 random cards with explicit suit cycle; chosen tied/no-suited-adviser suit; if normal allocation unavailable do not partially add it, sort all Dispossessed by suit, six from largest stack into world deck, return remaining suit stacks shuffled into matching Archive. Source supplies no separate largest-stack tie or special six-card-shortfall algorithm.')
row('Law8.5–8.8; errataChronicle aid; Playbook29–31','Q020 Q050 Q051 Q052 Q085 Q101','Chronicle removal eligibility, relic cleanup order, persistent state and deck rebuild.','Keys require all five Visions set aside, losing advisers plus regional discards with six unseen removal excluding winner advisers, Scepter saved, losing relic shuffle then faceup-site R refill before winner/Reliquary top stack, saved site order/attachments and current boards, ten+two top12/fifteen+three next18/remaining denizens, correct aid error, first Archive initialization and deferred setup prerequisite.')
row('Law9.1–9.6; Playbook31–32','Q040 Q041 Q042 Q043','Literal hierarchy, constrained components, private information and unprompted costs/promises.','Keys distinguish Law priority except SiteReference/nonitalic reminder priority, cannot over must/named ignore over both/must-if-able no penalty, unlimited secrets/dice but finite others with source shortfall, no bank/board cap, no excess placement/burn/sacrifice, private facedown/discard/world information versus public counts/board holdings, allowed adviser showing and lies, and no mixing adviser identities.')
row('Law10 Glossary; errataDraw/Enemy/Rule/You','Q009 Q011 Q015 Q033 Q065 Q067 Q069 Q081 Q089 Q090 Q096 Q097 Q098 Q099 Q100','Each operative glossary distinction must do work rather than be covered by an unrelated section label.','Keys directly test After immediate no intervening step; Burn default board to shared bank; next-region facedown ordered Discard with remote-card location and resource return; corrected Draw; Enemy/YourEnemy and bandits; optional Exchange; Force; Gain origins/shortfall; Give versus Take distinct defaults; Kill color bank and Sacrifice; Move/Swap legal restrictions without Play triggers; Peek versus public Reveal; Rule garrison versus pawn; Seize versus Recover. Removed You is replaced by side sharing with your site/board remaining individual.')
row('Site Reference p2 Opportunity/Homeland','Q053 Q092','Site income source/locality/timing and matching Homeland discard guard/reward procedure.','Q092 gives one token total from site at end Wake, optional, pawn required not remote rule, no bank substitution if empty. Q053 asks a different-suit discard and key expressly conditions reward on no same-suit card discarded there this turn; all printed reward classes and direct relic treating as Recover without normal action/site cost are tested.')
row('Site Reference p2 Coasts/NarrowPass','Q054 Q055','Travel gate versus Campaign gate and both endpoints for Coast shortcut.','Q054 requires origin Coast and destination Coast, fixed one and named NarrowPass ignore, rejects destination-only shortcut. Q055 requires travel from another region to Pass; Campaign cross-region targets add Pass unless attacker rules it; ruling does not cancel travel gate.')
row('Site Reference p2 Plains/Mountain/River/CharmingValley','Q061 Q062 Q063','Triggers cannot be reduced to mere site-name mentions.','Q061 tests any target at site including non-site target, mandatory +/- attack die even attacker rules. Q062 requires Muster from card there plus rule for extra warband, otherwise ordinary two. Q063 tests origin-based +1 Supply and spend-no-Supply override.')
row('Site Reference p2 ShroudedWood/BuriedGiant/HiddenPlace','Q056 Q057 Q060','Exhaustion, named ignore scope and destination priority under forced travel.','Q056 requires board-secret flip for travel/target, rejects general free-Supply bypass. Q057 gives Giant optional secret flip, no Supply, NarrowPass only, secret remains exhausted; no HiddenPlace ignore. Q060 gives Wood fixed two before modifiers, both named ignores, enemy ruler destination/Chancellor for Empire even forced, with banish free Supply but destination restriction retained.')
row('Site Reference p2 GreatSlum/Marshes/Tribunal','Q058 Q059 Q064','Remaining site powers: timed discard, pawn-local Search reduction and exact negotiation assets.','Q059 expressly permits first discard for play or move only, subject locks, not unrelated discard. Q058 requires one fewer drawn with pawn there, not remote rule, preserving Vision/empty stop. Q064 tests ruler-or-local access, favor/secrets now plus future actions in combination with any player, disputed breach coin flip and no invented relic/banner immediate exchange.')
